  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 19,
    "summary": "A prudent wife is from the Lord—He who lends to the poor lends to the Lord—It is better to be a poor man than to be a liar.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Better is the poor that walketh in his integrity, than he that is perverse in his lips, and is a fool.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "D&C 88:17; 104:16."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Prov. 28:6; Alma 27:27; D&C 124:20 (15, 20)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Also, that the soul be without knowledge, it is not good; and he that hasteth with his feet sinneth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "D&C 42:61; Abr. 1:2."
          },
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "TG Haste."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 22
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 47
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The foolishness of man perverteth his way: and his heart fretteth against the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Foolishness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wealth maketh many friends; but the poor is separated from his neighbour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "Prov. 14:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A false witness shall not be unpunished, and he that speaketh lies shall not escape.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Mosiah 13:23."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Lying."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Many will entreat the favour of the prince: and every man is a friend to him that giveth gifts.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Prov. 29:26; Alma 47:35."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "Matt. 5:46."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "All the brethren of the poor do hate him: how much more do his friends go far from him? he pursueth them with words, yet they are wanting to him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Prov. 18:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 109
          },
          {
            "start": 117,
            "end": 120
          },
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 129
          },
          {
            "start": 138,
            "end": 145
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that getteth wisdom loveth his own soul: he that keepeth understanding shall find good.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A false witness shall not be unpunished, and he that speaketh lies shall perish.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "TG Punish."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "2 Ne. 9:34."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Delight is not seemly for a fool; much less for a servant to have rule over princes.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "Prov. 30:22 (21–22); Eccl. 10:7 (6–7)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The discretion of a man deferreth his anger; and it is his glory to pass over a transgression.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Rashness."
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Anger."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "TG Glory."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "TG Transgress."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The king’s wrath is as the roaring of a lion; but his favour is as dew upon the grass.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "Prov. 20:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A foolish son is the calamity of his father: and the contentions of a wife are a continual dropping.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Fatherhood."
          },
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "Prov. 21:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 90,
            "text": "Prov. 27:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "House and riches are the inheritance of fathers: and a prudent wife is from the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG Prudence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Slothfulness casteth into a deep sleep; and an idle soul shall suffer hunger.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "TG Laziness; Procrastination."
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Idleness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that keepeth the commandment keepeth his own soul; but he that despiseth his ways shall die.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Prov. 13:13; Luke 11:28; D&C 1:32."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 57
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that hath pity upon the poor lendeth unto the Lord; and that which he hath given will he pay him again.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Compassion; Generosity."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Mosiah 4:16 (16–18)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Chasten thy son while there is hope, and let not thy soul spare for his crying.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "TG Chastening."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man of great wrath shall suffer punishment: for if thou deliver him, yet thou must do it again.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "Morm. 8:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Hear counsel, and receive instruction, that thou mayest be wise in thy latter end.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Edification."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There are many devices in a man’s heart; nevertheless the counsel of the Lord, that shall stand.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "Isa. 46:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 9
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The desire of a man is his kindness: and a poor man is better than a liar.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Kindness."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "TG Lying."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 22
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The fear of the Lord tendeth to life: and he that hath it shall abide satisfied; he shall not be visited with evil.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Reverence."
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "Prov. 10:16; 11:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 28
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 57
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A slothful man hideth his hand in his bosom, and will not so much as bring it to his mouth again.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Laziness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 37
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Smite a scorner, and the simple will beware: and reprove one that hath understanding, and he will understand knowledge.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Prov. 21:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 89
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that wasteth his father, and chaseth away his mother, is a son that causeth shame, and bringeth reproach.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "Prov. 20:20; Mosiah 13:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 31
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Cease, my son, to hear the instruction that causeth to err from the words of knowledge.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "1 Ne. 8:34 (33–34); Mosiah 2:37 (33, 37)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "An ungodly witness scorneth judgment: and the mouth of the wicked devoureth iniquity.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Judgments are prepared for scorners, and stripes for the back of fools.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "IE flogging. Prov. 10:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
